  "content": "{\"rationale\":\"Algebraically simplify the update: new_v-old_v = beta*(v-old_v), so updated = old + k*beta*(v-old_v). This eliminates one full (ROWS,128) matrix multiply-by-k and one add/subtract, plus the separate new_v vector op, reducing arithmetic per element while remaining mathematically exact (well within atol=rtol=0.01).\",\"replacements\":[{\"old\":\"    old_v = tl.sum(old * k[None, :], 1)\\n    new_v = beta * v + (1. - beta) * old_v\\n    updated = old - k[None, :] * old_v[:, None] + k[None, :] * new_v[:, None]\\n    output = tl.sum(updated * q[None, :], 1) * SCALE\",\"new\":\"    old_v = tl.sum(old * k[None, :], 1)\\n    delta = beta * (v - old_v)\\n    updated = old + k[None, :] * delta[:, None]\\n    output = tl.sum(updated * q[None, :], 1) * SCALE\"}]}"
